    "['remote-ip [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'neighbor 3.3.3.9 remote-as [AS_NUMBER]', 'parent_command': ['mpls ldp neighbor 3.3.3.9'], 'root': 'mpls ldp neighbor 3.3.3.9', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"##\\nneighbor 3.3.3.9 remote-as [AS_NUMBER]\\n##\\n\\nNote: In Cisco's MPLS LDP configuration, you would typically specify the neighbor's LSR-ID (3.3.3.9 in this case) under LDP router configuration with a remote AS number. The exact AS number would need to be filled in based on your network's BGP configuration. \\n\\nFor pure LDP peering without BGP, the Cisco equivalent would be:\\n##\\nmpls ldp neighbor 3.3.3.9 targeted\\n##\\n\\nChoose the appropriate version based on whether you're using BGP or pure LDP for the L2VPN setup.\", 'trans_template': 'neighbor 3.3.3.9 remote-as [AS_NUMBER]'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'mpls ldp neighbor 3.3.3.9 targeted', 'parent_command': ['mpls ldp neighbor 3.3.3.9'], 'root': 'mpls ldp neighbor 3.3.3.9', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"##\\nneighbor 3.3.3.9 remote-as [AS_NUMBER]\\n##\\n\\nNote: In Cisco's MPLS LDP configuration, you would typically specify the neighbor's LSR-ID (3.3.3.9 in this case) under LDP router configuration with a remote AS number. The exact AS number would need to be filled in based on your network's BGP configuration. \\n\\nFor pure LDP peering without BGP, the Cisco equivalent would be:\\n##\\nmpls ldp neighbor 3.3.3.9 targeted\\n##\\n\\nChoose the appropriate version based on whether you're using BGP or pure LDP for the L2VPN setup.\", 'trans_template': 'mpls ldp neighbor 3.3.3.9 targeted'}]]": 1,
