    "['mpls l2vpn qos cir [parameter1] pir [parameter2]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'service-policy output POLICY_NAME', 'parent_command': ['interface [parameter1]'], 'root': 'interface [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the translated Cisco equivalent command for the HUAWEI `mpls l2vpn qos cir 2000 pir 3000` configuration:\\n\\n##\\nservice-policy output POLICY_NAME\\n##\\n\\nNote: In Cisco, you would need to first define a policy-map with the corresponding CIR (2000 kbps) and PIR (3000 kbps) values, then apply it to the interface. The actual policy-map configuration would look something like this (not requested in your question, but for completeness):\\n\\n```\\npolicy-map POLICY_NAME\\n class class-default\\n  police cir 2000000 pir 3000000 conform-action transmit exceed-action transmit violate-action drop\\n```\\n\\nThe HUAWEI command sets QoS parameters for the L2VPN service with Committed Information Rate (2000 kbps) and Peak Information Rate (3000 kbps), while Cisco implements this through MQC (Modular QoS CLI) with policy-maps.\", 'trans_template': 'service-policy output POLICY_NAME'}]]": 1,
